# Every text file checks out LF on every platform. The repository stores LF
# only, the build runs in Linux containers, and GNU patch (patches/*.patch,
# applied with patch -p1 by the Dockerfile and the workflow) refuses a target
# whose line endings differ from the patch, which a CRLF checkout under
# core.autocrlf would hand it. Batch files are the one exception: cmd.exe
# wants CRLF. Refresh an existing checkout with: git checkout-index -a -f
* text=auto eol=lf

*.c       text
*.cpp     text
*.h       text
*.s       text
*.sct     text
*.ld      text
*.txt     text
*.xml     text
*.py      text
*.md      text
*.json    text
*.tmpl    text
*.dia     binary
*.elf     binary
*.bin     binary
*.exe     binary
*.bat     text eol=crlf
